[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first, and our
tenants write the day first. Its own table already disagrees. Read report by report, the merged
reports show two problems, and the queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket now. The parser fix leaves the form open.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/luca-gugs/what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/luca-gugs/what-it-shows/issues/2',
  }}
/>

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the report shows a day/month swap ("Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July"), and
  it came in by app or email, or through a booking-v2 form. The shared parser read a day-first date
  month first.
- **`hint`**: the same swap, but it came in through a booking-v3 form. That form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month first, and the form then reads the
  date the tenant's way, day first. The fix belongs in the form, so the parser fix does not touch it.

A few `parser` reports read as a one-day move, not a swap ("Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday";
the desk lists them in `desk-notes.json`). By tenant and channel they are the parser's, so they are
counted there. Check them again when the parser fix ships.

The subject line does not tell the two apart: most subjects turn up under both. Read the tenant, the
channel and the booking form.

## How the count was made

1. Take the export of #4471 and keep one report per id. The ticket system exports pages that
   overlap, so some reports come twice.
2. Place each report by its tenant (locale and booking form) and its channel, as `causes.ts` does.
   The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not the cause.

The numbers on this page are computed from the export when the page renders (`ProblemTable`, on
`causes.ts`), so they follow the data as the desk keeps merging.

## What this changes

- #4471 is not "known, one fix queued". The queued fix covers `parser`. `hint` needs its own fix in
  the booking-v3 form, and its own owner.
- Merging on the subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) cannot keep
  these apart. That decision stays as it is; a new record should replace it.

